{"name":"Rock Garden","hex":"#465448","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rock garden","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of rockery.","A rock-strewn path, part of a mountain biking racecourse"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rock_garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alpine garden","blocks":[{"text":"An alpine garden is a domestic or botanical garden, or more often a part of a larger garden, specializing in the collection and cultivation of alpine plants growing naturally at high altitudes around the world, such as in the Caucasus, Pyrenees, Rocky Mountains, Alps, Himalayas and Andes. It is one of the most common types of rock garden."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Alps-Garden_Schachen.jpg/330px-Alps-Garden_Schachen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpine_garden","wikidata":"Q1429180"},{"title":"Rock garden","blocks":[{"text":"A rock garden, also known as a rockery and formerly as a rockwork, is a garden, or more often a part of a garden, with a landscaping framework of rocks, stones, and gravel, with planting appropriate to this setting. Usually these are small Alpine plants that need relatively little soil or water. Western rock gardens are often divided into alpine gardens, scree gardens on looser, smaller stones, and other rock gardens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Rock_Garden_at_Wisley-geograph-2580831-by-Josie-Campbell.jpg/330px-Rock_Garden_at_Wisley-geograph-2580831-by-Josie-Campbell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_garden","wikidata":"Q1141231"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden","wikidata":"Q1107656"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Alps-Garden_Schachen.jpg/500px-Alps-Garden_Schachen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Alps-Garden_Schachen.jpg/1280px-Alps-Garden_Schachen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Alps-Garden_Schachen.jpg/500px-Alps-Garden_Schachen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An alpinum adjacent to the King's House on Schachen in Garmisch-Partenkirchen, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlps-Garden_Schachen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/BF_alpine_gardens_1.JPG/500px-BF_alpine_gardens_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/BF_alpine_gardens_1.JPG/1280px-BF_alpine_gardens_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/BF_alpine_gardens_1.JPG/500px-BF_alpine_gardens_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Betty Ford Alpine Gardens","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABF_alpine_gardens_1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Bielefeld_Botanischer_Garten_Alpinum_1.jpg/500px-Bielefeld_Botanischer_Garten_Alpinum_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki